---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Glowcard from '~/components/glowcard.astro';

import '~/assets/styles/glow.css';
import '~/assets/styles/tailwind.css';

import lucienSvgUrl from '~/assets/lucien.svg?url';
---

<Layout>
  <section id="story" class="pt-10">
    <Glowcard>
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4">
        <!-- Intro -->
        <div class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-5xl font-extrabold mb-3">
            <span class="bg-clip-text text-transparent bg-mona bg-[length:200%_200%] animate-gradient-move">
              The Story
            </span>
          </h2>
          <p class="text-lg font-medium opacity-90">
            Every project starts somewhere. This one grew out of moments shared with friends.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <!-- Chapter 1 -->
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-60 mb-2">Chapter 1</p>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Creating moments together</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90">
              Long before The Mona existed, there was Lucien.
              A small creation meant to add a bit of fun, light, and chaos to moments with friends.
              Nothing complicated — just something that made people smile and come together.
            </p>

            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90 mt-3">
              Lucien became part of those shared times: cafés, gatherings, inside jokes.
              A reminder that simple ideas can turn into great memories.
            </p>

            <img
              src={lucienSvgUrl}
              alt="Lucien"
              class="mt-6 w-full max-w-sm mx-auto opacity-95 drop-shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(255,255,255,0.15)]"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>

          <hr class="border-white/10" />

          <!-- Chapter 2 -->
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-60 mb-2">Chapter 2</p>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">A new spark at a BBQ</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90">
              During a BBQ with friends, the conversation drifted — as it often does —
              toward ideas, jokes, and half-serious thoughts.
              Buttons, lights, interaction… nothing fully formed, just possibilities.
            </p>

            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90 mt-3">
              Someone casually said, “Yeah… Greg could probably build something like that.”
              It wasn’t a plan or a request, just a passing comment.
              But it planted a new seed.
            </p>
          </div>

          <hr class="border-white/10" />

          <!-- Chapter 3 -->
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-60 mb-2">Chapter 3</p>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">From a feeling to a new idea</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90">
              That moment made me reflect on what I enjoyed most about Lucien:
              not the object itself, but the shared experience around it.
            </p>

            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90 mt-3">
              I started thinking about what something new could be —
              something playful, interactive, and open-ended.
              Not a replacement for Lucien, but a next step.
            </p>
          </div>

          <hr class="border-white/10" />

<!-- Chapter 4 -->
<div>
  <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-60 mb-2">Chapter 4</p>
  <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Why “The Mona”?</h3>

  <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90 mb-4">
    As this new idea began to take shape, it became clear that it needed its own identity.
    When searching for a name, I wanted something that reflected a meaningful moment of renewal
    and inspiration in my life — a shift from simply building things to truly feeling connected
    to the act of creating.
  </p>

  <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90 mb-4">
    *The Mona* represents a period where small moments regained their beauty,
    and where the simple act of creating felt alive again.
    It marks a time when inspiration quietly returned,
    bringing with it a renewed sense of presence, curiosity,
    and intention in what I was building.
  </p>

  <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90">
    This project captures the essence of that rediscovery.
    It transforms a brief but impactful chapter into a creative expression
    of gratitude and forward momentum.
    While moments pass and paths change, what remains is the growth they spark.
    *The Mona* is a tribute to that process — holding onto what helped me move forward
    and shaping it into something that can continue to inspire
    and create meaningful moments for others.
  </p>
</div>


          <hr class="border-white/10" />

          <!-- Chapter 5 -->
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-60 mb-2">Chapter 5</p>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">From moments to possibilities</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed opacity-90">
              Today, The Mona continues to grow.
              It’s an evolving project, shaped by curiosity and the same desire
              that started it all: creating small moments worth sharing with others.
            </p>

 
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Glowcard>
  </section>
</Layout>
